The Buddha gave many of his talks.

17
00:01:53,275 --> 00:02:07,896
Now, on that occasion, the Venerable Chanda was afflicted, suffering and gravely ill. And when it was evening, the Venerable Sariputta rose from meditation, went to the Venerable Mahachandra and said to him, French Chandra, let's go and visit Chanda and ask about his illness.

18
00:02:09,276 --> 00:02:20,631
And then after they do so, and after the exchange greetings with him, when the Curtis and Andy Bull talk was finished, they sat to one side and said, I hope you're getting well, friend Chanda, says Sariputta.

19
00:02:20,651 --> 00:02:21,812
I hope you're comfortable.

20
00:02:22,493 --> 00:02:32,105
I hope your painful feelings are subsiding and not increasing, and that they're subsiding, not that increase is apparent.

21
00:02:33,807 --> 00:02:36,752
So I hope you're getting well, and I hope it's obvious to you you're getting well.

22
00:02:37,643 --> 00:02:40,406
Venerable Buddha, I'm not getting well.

23
00:02:40,425 --> 00:02:41,347
I'm not comfortable.

24
00:02:41,927 --> 00:02:44,890
My painful feelings are increasing, not subsiding.

25
00:02:45,512 --> 00:02:49,896
The increase and not their subsiding is apparent to me.

26
00:02:51,057 --> 00:02:52,299
I shall use the knife.

27
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:55,443
So this is one way of saying he's going to commit suicide.

28
00:02:56,584 --> 00:02:58,045
I have no desire to live.

29
00:02:59,647 --> 00:03:02,110
Let the Venerable Channa not use the knife.

30
00:03:02,471 --> 00:03:03,931
Let the Venerable Channa live.

31
00:03:05,334 --> 00:03:07,295
We want the Venerable Channa to live.

32
00:03:07,461 --> 00:03:14,352
If he lacks suitable food, I'll go in search of suitable food for him.

33
00:03:14,372 --> 00:03:18,337
If he lacks suitable medicine, I'll go in search of suitable medicine for him.

34
00:03:18,878 --> 00:03:21,923
If he lacks proper attendant, I will attend him.

35
00:03:21,943 --> 00:03:24,306
Let the Venerable Channa not use the knife.

36
00:03:25,027 --> 00:03:28,133
So here's Sariputta pleading with him.

37
00:03:28,152 --> 00:03:34,481
Friend Channa, it is not that I do not have suitable food or a proper attendant, but rather...

38
00:03:34,849 --> 00:03:47,165
that the teacher who is long worshipped by me with love, not without love, for it is proper for the disciple to worship the teacher with love and not without love.

39
00:03:47,986 --> 00:03:53,933
Friends, Sariputta, remember this, the Bhikkhu Channa will use the knife blamelessly.

40
00:03:53,973 --> 00:04:04,046
So in other words, it would be a dishonor to the teacher to do something which would disgrace him, to do something which he would definitely tell you not to do.

41
00:04:04,532 --> 00:04:09,177
But Chanda says, no, I will commit suicide in a blameless way.

42
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:14,062
We would ask the Venerable Chanda certain questions.

43
00:04:15,424 --> 00:04:19,908
By the way, the fact that he said blamelessly is suggesting he's fully liberated.

44
00:04:21,930 --> 00:04:30,699
Because there is another occasion where an Arahant, who is also in great pain from illness, says to the Buddha, I'm going to take the knife.

45
00:04:30,778 --> 00:04:31,839
That's how they would put it.

46
00:04:32,343 --> 00:04:36,148
And the Buddha says, do as you see fit.

47
00:04:36,752 --> 00:04:39,146
The Buddha wouldn't take moral decisions for other people.

48
00:04:41,776 --> 00:04:51,307
Frank Chandler, do you regard the eye, eye consciousness and things cognizable through eye consciousness as mine, this I am, and this is myself?

49
00:04:51,728 --> 00:04:55,733
And he goes through all the senses and the heart mind.

50
00:04:56,112 --> 00:05:03,362
And of course, the question is, is there still any identity within you with the psychophysical organism?

51
00:05:04,523 --> 00:05:13,833
And his reply is, I regard that the I and I consciousness, things cognizable through on all that are not mine, not I, not myself.

52
00:05:14,074 --> 00:05:16,541
So he's saying that he is.

53
00:05:19,069 --> 00:05:24,098
And then Sariputta says, what have you seen?

54
00:05:24,197 --> 00:05:25,420
What have you directly known?

55
00:05:25,439 --> 00:05:31,228
So he's questioning him now because he's not sure that this monk is actually fully liberated.

56
00:05:31,608 --> 00:05:34,392
You can overestimate your attainments.

57
00:05:35,975 --> 00:05:36,817
What have you seen?

58
00:05:36,877 --> 00:05:40,682
What have you directly known by your direct experience?

59
00:05:40,702 --> 00:05:41,584
This is the point you see.

60
00:05:42,846 --> 00:05:51,716
And he replies, it is through seeing cessation, through directly knowing cessation in the eye, and so on and so forth.

61
00:05:51,735 --> 00:06:02,607
So, in other words, it's the point where the whole of the psychophysical organism, as it were, drops away and you are left with the Buddha within, right?

62
00:06:03,127 --> 00:06:04,769
That's what he's saying, cessation.

63
00:06:05,951 --> 00:06:10,896
Now, when this was said, Mahaconda also doesn't believe that he's actually fully liberated.

